  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_031 (multimodal, scVI_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc. However, the image-only ResNet50 baseline was extremely weak (0.208), raising uncertainty about whether the image modality is contributing meaningful signal or merely adding noise that the weighted fusion partially compensates for. Question: config_037 isolates a single variable—upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet ViT-L—while keeping the rest of the pipeline identical to config_031 (scVI_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted). This directly tests whether a stronger visual representation unlocks additional signal from the image modality. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is a clean one-factor comparison against our current best, so any performance change can be attributed to image encoder quality. (2) The answer has high strategic value: if ViT-L substantially improves over ResNet50, the image modality is a genuine contributor and further multimodal exploration is warranted; if it does not, we can conclude the image channel is not informative and redirect budget toward RNA-side improvements. (3) It avoids changing multiple variables simultaneously (unlike config_039, which would also change aggregation), preserving interpretability under a tight budget."
}

